url: "https://huggingface.co/kabartay/fintfm-binary"
abstract: >-
  An in-context tabular classifier for corporate credit risk, pretrained only on
  synthetic data and never on a real table. Prediction is a single forward pass with
  the user's table supplied as context: by default there are no gradient steps at
  fit time and no per-dataset tuning, and fine-tuning is opt-in. The repository is
  built around a numbered measurement log and a claims ledger that record
  retractions and superseded results as prominently as confirmations. On
  TabArena-Lite (one fold, all 51 datasets, none excluded), FinTFM with a trained
  linear readout scores 1,022.6 Elo, 108th of 119 methods, above RandomForest
  (default) at 1,000 but inside the Elo interval; the zero-shot model, submitted to
  TabArena on 27 binary datasets, placed 94th of 95. On real corporate-default
  panels its discrimination loses to gradient boosting (0.20 against 0.40 mean
  average precision for untuned CatBoost on V4FinBench), and it is below logistic
  regression on four further credit datasets. Calibration was among the best
  measured for an earlier architecture; it is not claimed for the published
  checkpoint.
keywords:
  - tabular foundation model
  - in-context learning
  - prior-fitted networks
  - credit risk
  - synthetic data
